			<div class="content" id="post-content-3684016">
									

<p>I finally decided to take the plunge.</p>
<p>This is part of the Alchemy Series, though at first glance it may not appear so. Pay close attention to the fancy formatting.</p>
<p>Thanks go to everyone who took a look at this, and gave me feedback on the forums.</p>
<p>The formatting serves two puposes:</p>
<ol>
<li>This is much more computer-esque which has always bothered me that the Foundation is hypercompetent at almost everything, but apparently web design.</li>
<li>The formatting allows for several key pieces of information to be conveyed.</li>
</ol>
<p>Now to you, I pose a question. Where have you heard the name &quot;Ledenoff&quot; before?</p>
<p>EDIT: This theme is publically available at ccastellano.github.io/magnus-theme.css To use it on your pages:</p>
<p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[module]]</span><br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;@import&#32;url(http://ccastellano.github.io/magnus-theme.css)</span><br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[/module]]</span></p>
<p>From there, you can use all the div id's that correspond with these components.</p>

