<p>See, this is pretty much paint-by-the-numbers SCP writing. All of these, on their own and together, have been hashed and rehashed endlessly already. Your basic anomaly &#8212; magic makes software companies bureaucratize themselves to a halt &#8212; is nothing to write home about, so you're not doing it any favors by plugging it into a generic story.</p>
<p>So I guess to answer your question of &quot;Where exactly would this have gone?&quot;, I would say &quot;literally anywhere unexpected&quot;. There are no curveballs in this piece, nothing that forced me to reevaluate what I'd already read, nothing truly unsettling or weird&#8230; It only goes somewhere in the sense that moving from your bedroom to the kitchen is going somewhere.</p>

